## Report

```md
# Project Report

# Carbon Emission Estimator for Supply Chains

## Introduction
Carbon emissions from supply chains are increasing due to transportation, logistics, warehousing, and manufacturing operations.  
This project uses Machine Learning techniques to estimate carbon emissions and provide sustainability recommendations.

---

## Objective
The objectives of this project are:
- Predict carbon emissions in supply chains
- Analyze sustainability factors
- Suggest methods to reduce emissions
- Build an interactive prediction system

---

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Streamlit
- Scikit-learn
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib

---

## Dataset Description
The dataset contains information related to supply chain operations and sustainability factors.

Features include:
- Supplier Count
- Lead Time
- Energy Consumption
- Renewable Energy Usage
- Recycling Rate
- Green Packaging Usage
- Operational Efficiency
- Customer Satisfaction
- Supply Chain Risk

Target Variable:
- Carbon Emissions (kg CO2e)

---

## Methodology

### Data Preprocessing
- Handling missing values
- Feature engineering
- Data encoding
- Feature scaling

### Machine Learning Models
The following regression algorithms were tested:
- Linear Regression
- Ridge Regression
- Random Forest
- Extra Trees
- Gradient Boosting

The best model was selected based on performance metrics.

---

## System Working
1. User enters supply chain details
2. Input data is processed
3. Trained ML model predicts carbon emissions
4. System displays:
   - Predicted emissions
   - Emission level
   - Recommendations
   - Comparison charts

---

## Features
- Interactive web application
- Real-time prediction
- Sustainability insights
- Emission comparison graphs
- Improvement simulation

---

## Results
The system successfully predicts carbon emissions and suggests improvement strategies such as:
- Increasing renewable energy usage
- Improving recycling rate
- Using green packaging
- Reducing supply chain risk
- Improving operational efficiency

---

## Conclusion
This project shows how Machine Learning can help organizations improve sustainable supply chain management by predicting and reducing carbon emissions.

---

